  "worked_solution": "First, we apply the constant factor rule and take the coefficient $5$ out of the integral. Then we compute the integral of $\\frac{1}{x},$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{5}{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =5\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5\\operatorname{ln}\u2061|x|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
